1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
SMT World: Clock In. Call the market once a day against an AI trading agent. Solana keeps the score.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:15,000
It's a native Android app. The APK comes from the GitHub release, built by GitHub Actions from the public repo.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:24,767
Once a day I call one coin UP or DOWN for the next 4 hours. Eight coins, with live prices from Binance.

4
00:00:24,767 --> 00:00:34,133
I call BTC UP. SMT's own call on BTC stays hidden until mine is on chain, so it can't steer me.

5
00:00:34,133 --> 00:00:41,600
The app builds one devnet transaction and hands it to my wallet through Mobile Wallet Adapter.

6
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:48,667
Solflare shows the transaction and I approve it. The app never sees a private key.

7
00:00:48,667 --> 00:00:58,800
It's on chain. Now SMT shows its call on BTC: sitting out at 24% conviction, leaning DOWN, with every advisor's vote and reason.

8
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:07,800
SMT is scored only when it really calls LONG or SHORT. Sitting out isn't a prediction, so it isn't graded.

9
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:19,867
One transaction, two memos. The first holds my call and SMT's, signed by my wallet. The second points to a shared registry address that every Clock In names.

10
00:01:19,867 --> 00:01:32,333
My history is read back from devnet, so a new phone loses nothing. Four hours later each call is graded on the market price at or after that moment.

11
00:01:32,333 --> 00:01:41,700
My first week: 0 right of 3. The market won. SMT sat out all three, so it has no score yet.

12
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:52,600
The leaderboard reads every player's calls straight from that registry address. No server of mine, no database. Right now it's just me: it's launch week.

13
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:59,300
Anyone can check it on Solana Explorer: the registry's history lists every Clock In.

14
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:13,667
The SMT tab shows what the trading agent thinks of all 8 coins right now, and opens SMT World, the full web app. With a wallet, it unlocks after my call for the day.

15
00:02:13,667 --> 00:02:27,667
SKR, the Solana Mobile token, is a ninth coin to call. SMT doesn't trade it, so that one is just me against the market. The app reads my SKR balance on mainnet, read-only.

16
00:02:27,667 --> 00:02:33,200
Any call can be shared as a card, with its transaction.

17
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:42,200
A home-screen widget keeps the streak in view, and a 9:00 reminder fires only if I haven't clocked in yet.

18
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:51,200
Built October 7 to 12, 2026. Try it on an Android phone: the APK is on the GitHub release.
